    "content": "Although LLMs can often solve such problems by writing or calling basic search code, our goal hereis to isolate their intrinsic planning and state-tracking abilities without such tools. We therefore aska concrete question: how well can LLMs plan and reason over an evolving state when they cannotrely on code execution or other external tools? To answer this, we use the standard 8-puzzle and askmodels to solve random configurations of the game. The 8-puzzle requires models to maintain anaccurate representation of the board, obey strict move validity constraints, and choose moves thateventually reach a goal state. We measure not only whether a puzzle is solved but also how and whyruns terminate when they fail, to understand the limits of model performance on this type of task.",
